      "name": "Ricard's Division",
      "formation": "8th Division, VI Corps (Marmont)",
      "side": "French",
      "summary": "Marmont's division, caught with the rest of his corps on the open plain by the allied cavalry on its way to Paris, and driven back with heavy loss.",
      "notes": [
        "Built from A Clash of Eagles' French 1812 list, the nearest to 1814: there is no list for the army Napoleon fought with in France, of the veterans of 1813, conscripts called up that winter and battalions drawn from depots across the Empire.",
        "Nafziger has no order of battle for Fère-Champenoise. Marmont's and Mortier's corps are from his return of the army on the Aisne on 17 March, eight days before, with Marmont's battalions from his 12 March return.",
        "On Nafziger's return of 17 March the division had 940 men, in Pelleport's and Clavel's brigades; its battalions here are those of 12 March.",
        "After Athies the division had about 650 men in seven battalions, fifty to a hundred and sixty each. They are shown at full size; the list's Small upgrade would suit them all.",
        "Nafziger gives the battalions without brigades; they are split here, light and line, as the list takes them.",
        "A brigade of four light battalions, where the list takes three regiments and one light regiment in the division, shows as a historical departure.",
        "Commanders are at Staff Rating 8, the default for historical forces."
